  annotation "note_1771592173396_1", anchor: "The broader toll is recorded as seventeen", text: "Three named candidates preserved in accord preambles because their deaths were diplomatically useful. Fourteen unnamed. From a structural collapse the ice at that depth records only as vibration — not bodies, not individual thermal signatures, just shearing force. Fourteen unnamed dead in a number one short of round, from a source that cannot distinguish a falling penguin from a falling stone. I do not trust this figure and I said so in the main text as gently as the prose would bear.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771592173396_2", anchor: "The Nightshelf were, by all accounts, unsurprised", text: "'Unsurprised' undersells it. Nyla's predecessor — and the amended histories will not tell you this, but the administrative ice is unambiguous — was Aurora-born. Not Nightshelf-raised, not recruited from neutral courier lines. An Aurora penguin running Nightshelf shadow operations with access to the constellation families' internal disputes. The Nightshelf did not anticipate the fracture. They watched it develop through embedded sources. That I wrote 'by all accounts, unsurprised' rather than stating this is a concession to diplomatic access I can no longer justify keeping.", type: :correction, display: :full
